# Secrets — never commit
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem

# Internal audit docs — never publish.
# NOTE: SECURITY.md is deliberately NOT ignored — that path is reserved for the
# public vulnerability-reporting policy. The internal audit ledger lives in
# docs/internal/ instead.
#
# AUDIT-*.md covers the class, not one filename: any review tool pointed at this
# repo writes its findings somewhere, and an unreviewed findings file in a repo
# that is about to go public is the worst possible thing to commit by accident.
# Phase 0 found exactly this — a REVIEW.md protected by nothing, one `git add -A`
# from publishing a list of open criticals.
REVIEW.md
AUDIT-*.md
docs/internal/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage

# Local tooling state
.planning/

# Internal build history — kept on disk, never published.
# 23 files of design specs and implementation plans written during the build.
# Not setup docs, not product docs; the README's own marker said "nothing here
# is required to run the system". Untracked 2026-08-04 (audit finding 10).
# ⚠️ Untracking removes it from the tree, NOT from history — 45 earlier commits
# still contain it. See the audit note if that matters for the public mirror.
docs/superpowers/
seeds/docs/superpowers/
